# event-emitter API — event-driven account → snapshot flow
# Flow: POST /accounts creates an account and EMITS 'snapshots.generate' on
# the global EventEmitter2 bus; SnapshotsService (@OnEvent listener) reacts
# and records a snapshot. The two modules never call each other directly.

### 1. Create an account — stores it AND emits snapshots.generate.
###    Returns 201 with an empty body (handler returns nothing).
POST http://localhost:3000/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Bob",
  "amount": 1000
}

### 2. Snapshots — lists snapshots produced by the event listener.
###    Empty [] until a POST /accounts has fired the event (in-memory state).
GET http://localhost:3000/snapshots
